// EXPECT: FAIL
// An assignment to a variable whose type has no Syntax anywhere in its
// supertype chain must be rejected: matched_literal() (adlparser.h) used to
// fall back to accepting any quoted-string-or-numeric-looking token in this
// case - the fallback that let ADL bootstrap String/Integer/etc before any
// Syntax existed to describe them. That fallback is gone; only the
// self-typed-field special case in ADLStoreSink::lookup_syntax() (adlstore.h,
// see 35_syntax_self_typed_ok.adl) still lets a literal through when the
// variable's own type has no Syntax. Message has neither, so this must fail.
TOP {
	Message:;
	Trail Text: Message = 'text';		// Faulty: Message has no Syntax to conform to
}
